o the forecast sits near the Safe R boundary.", "watch": "A late influx of outside spending against Wied or a polling surprise showing Crosson within single digits would move this toward Likely R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tony Wied (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Tony Wied seeks a second term in Wisconsin's 8th District, a seat with an R+8 partisan lean, against Democrat Rick Crosson. Wied ran unopposed in his primary and has raised roughly $1.09 million, while Crosson, who emerged from a three-way Democratic primary, has raised about $67,000. No outside spending has been reported on either side.\n\nNo general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert judgment. Raters overwhelmingly call the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Wied about an 88% chance of winning. Local coverage has focused on issue contrasts, including Wied's positions on tariffs and the farm bill, but nothing suggests a competitive contest. The forecast expects Wied to win by a wide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0582, "margin": -10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.066, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0472, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0325, "margin": -13.0}]}